# Go backend boundaries

Full docs: `docs/backend/architecture.md`, `docs/backend/layers.md`, `docs/backend/coding-standards.md`.

## Hard rules

- `chem` is the simulation library. Catalog, reactions, `World.Tick`, `DemoWorld`, and `ParcelView` live there.
- `cmd/web` is HTTP only: mutex, routes, frame JSON, embed `dist`. No new chemistry.
- `cmd/sandbox` prints ticks only. No HTTP, no catalog edits.
- Import one way: `cmd/*` → `chem`. Never the reverse. Never import `web/` from Go for simulation.
- Frame JSON (`tick`, `mass`, `parcels` / `ParcelView` tags) stays in sync with `web/src/types.ts` when changed; prefer not to change it.
- Plain comments; do not invent chemistry outside `DefaultCatalog`. Do not weaken physicist/chemist vetoes in adapters.
